---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaPair from "../components/CtaPair.astro";
import FinalCta from "../components/FinalCta.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";

const title = "Custom AI Systems for Miami Businesses | Launchline Design";
const description =
  "Custom AI for Miami businesses, from a single chatbot to full workflow automation. From $3,500 setup and from $997 a month. Fixed-scope proposal.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="From one chatbot to the operation"
    title="AI built around the way your office already works."
    lede="Internal assistants and agents built around your workflows. Custom starts at $3,500 to set up and $997 a month, after a discovery session and a written, fixed-scope proposal."
    crumbs={[
      { href: "/", label: "Home" },
      { href: "/custom-ai", label: "Custom AI" },
    ]}
  >
    <CtaPair loomHref="/demo#custom-demo" />
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap stack" style="max-width: 44rem">
      <h2>What Custom includes</h2>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>End-to-end workflow automation, from intake through follow-up</li>
        <li>CRM and practice-management integrations, named in the proposal</li>
        <li>Bilingual English and Spanish intake by phone, text, and chat</li>
        <li>Internal tools: assistants, document drafting, and reporting</li>
        <li>A discovery session and a written scope before build starts</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These are categories of work Launchline will propose. They are not case studies, and this site does not claim a measured result for any of them. If a client later approves a result, it will be published by name on the homepage. That space is empty today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap cards">
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>A single chatbot</h3>
        <p>Trained on your pages, your prices, and the sentences you refuse to let it say. Often the first custom piece, before the rest of the workflow.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Intake to follow-up</h3>
        <p>The call, the CRM record, the reminder, and the review request as one path. Multi-location offices and high call volume are the usual reason to leave Growth.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Tools for the team</h3>
        <p>An assistant that drafts from your own documents, or a report that lands on a schedule. Internal only. Not a public claim about savings.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Scoped in writing. Not a retainer that wanders.</h2>
      <p>
        Custom is for multi-location or high-volume businesses ready to automate past the front desk. The quote is confirmed on the call. “From $3,500” and “from $997 a month” are starting points, not a ceiling and not a surprise invoice.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you only need one automation — a form into a CRM, a nightly summary, a bilingual after-hours flow — a single custom automation starts at $750. You do not have to buy the whole system to fix one gap.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your accounts and data stay yours. Usage is billed at cost with no markup. Timeline depends on the scope. “As little as 7 days” applies to Starter and Growth, not to a custom build, unless the proposal says so.
      </p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/pricing">Compare Custom with Starter and Growth</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FinalCta />
</Base>
